.TH RANMA-TMUX-SHIM 1 "" "ranma 0.1.0" "ranma manual"
.SH NAME
ranma\-tmux\-shim \- Run COMMAND (your shell when left out) with a \fBtmux\fR on its PATH that answers in this ranma: \fBranma tmux\-shim \-\- claude\fR. See CONFIG.md
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBranma tmux\-shim\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run COMMAND (your shell when left out) with a \fBtmux\fR on its PATH that answers in this ranma: \fBranma tmux\-shim \-\- claude\fR. See CONFIG.md
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
The command and its arguments, after \fB\-\-\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBranma\fR(1)
